course: dictionary
lesson: 13116
title: Words for parts of a house
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A floorboard is one of the long, flat pieces of wood that join together to make a wooden floor. «The floorboards creaked as Sam crept across the room.» Creaked means made a long, squeaky sound, and the word floorboards tells you what made the sound: the wood under his feet.
explain: Look at the words around floorboard to work out its meaning. «A loose floorboard lifted under her foot.» Loose means not fixed down tightly, so a loose floorboard can move when you step on it. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence, a piece of floor or a piece of wall?
explain: Writers often use floorboards in stories. «The map was hidden under the floorboards.» Under tells you the map was below the floor, out of sight. In many stories, creaking floorboards show that someone is sneaking around and trying not to be heard.
fact: A floorboard is one long, flat piece of wood in a wooden floor.
fact: Floorboards are common in old houses.
fact: «Creaking floorboards» means floorboards that make a squeaky, groaning sound when you step on them.
fact: «A loose floorboard» means a board that is not fixed down tightly.
fact: «Under the floorboards» means in the space below the floor, out of sight.
exercise: «The floorboards creaked as Sam crept across the room.» What is a floorboard? | A piece of glass in a window | A wooden chair in the kitchen | *One of the long, flat pieces of wood that make a floor
exercise: «A loose floorboard lifted under her foot.» What does loose mean here? | Very tall and thin | Painted bright red | *Not fixed down tightly | Full of water
exercise: «The map was hidden under the floorboards.» Where was the map? | On the roof | On the table | *Under the floor, out of sight | In the bin
test: «The old house had wooden floorboards that shone in the sun.» What are the wooden floorboards? | Stones in the garden | Windows on the roof | Doors that open onto the garden | *Pieces of wood that make up the floor
test: Mia heard creaking floorboards in the hall at night. What might the creaking tell her? | The house is on fire | It is raining outside | The kettle is boiling | *Someone may be walking quietly where they should not be
exam: Which word means a floorboard that is not fixed down tightly? | Sweet | Happy | *Loose | Tall
